=== FIXED/REQUIRES ATTENTION: deduped_010_lccn ===
=== A record had more than one 010 (LCCN) field, or a single 010 with more
===   than one $a -- merged into exactly one 010. Every $a on the record is
===   compared with its whitespace stripped: if they all normalize the same,
===   the stripped value is kept; if two or more normalize to genuinely
===   different values, the best one is kept as $a (a value that is a valid
===   LCCN under LC's structure rules,
===   https://www.loc.gov/marc/lccn_structure.html, always beats one that is
===   not; among valid LCCNs the newest year wins, then the highest serial)
===   and the others are moved to $z (nothing is lost). NOTE: treating the
===   other LCCNs as canceled/invalid ($z) is a guess -- it has not been
===   verified that they are invalid, so each should be checked. Every $z
===   (Canceled/Invalid LCCN) and $b (NUCMC control number -- rare, treated
===   the same as $z) from every original 010 is carried onto the surviving
===   field, de-duplicated -- except a $z matching the surviving $a, which is
===   dropped as a contradiction.
